                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Largest, greatest (in magnitude), highest, most."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a285703a-9e0c-406e-9d83-3c02c7db8341",
                                                "sense_id": "96ce15fe-ab40-3cda-ba96-7819e04ec697",
                                                "text": "The organification of iodide in the thyroid gland was described using a second order rate constant (KthybindC, /nmol/L*hr/kg thyroid weight) fitted to provide thyroidal iodide stores near the maximal value, which increased with age."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14185123-7ce0-3fda-8c8e-49483c124aa0",
                                        "entry_id": "6fbc2504-d84f-39c3-a913-a833ac82682a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Larger than any previous term in the sequence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a sequence"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9c96484-b3d4-46cc-817b-8638c08495f6",
                                                "sense_id": "14185123-7ce0-3fda-8c8e-49483c124aa0",
                                                "text": "In the sequence (1, 2, 10, 5, 12, 6), the fifth term, f(5) = 12, is a maximal term, as each of the first 4 terms are smaller than 12."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb025472-197e-351b-9039-60f535de69cf",
                                        "entry_id": "6fbc2504-d84f-39c3-a913-a833ac82682a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Such that no other element is greater (with respect to the given partial order)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of an element of a poset"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fbfece3-fcc1-415e-9d80-0302815f0378",
                                                "sense_id": "eb025472-197e-351b-9039-60f535de69cf",
                                                "text": "With respect to the ordering induced by set-theoretic inclusion, the set #92;#123;#92;#123;2#92;#125;,#92;#123;1,2#92;#125;,#92;#123;2,3#92;#125;#92;#125; has two maximal elements: #92;#123;1,2#92;#125; and #92;#123;2,3#92;#125;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
